-----Original Message-----
From: Zack Almquist [mailto:almquist@uci.edu] 
Sent: Friday, April 20, 2012 12:07 PM
To: Tom
Subject: Re: [statnet_help] Text Vertex Attributes

Hi Tom,

Here is a quick example (if I am understanding your question
correctly) of one solution for adding vertex attributes based on their
label. Hopefully this will help, and let me know if there is anything
unclear in my example.

Best,

-- Zack
---------------------------------------------------------
Zack W.  Almquist
Doctoral Student, Department of Sociology University of California, Irvine
Web: http://www.socsci.uci.edu/~almquist


----------------

library(sna)
library(network)

net<-network(rgraph(10))
net%v%"vertex.names"<-c("a","b","c","d","e","f","g","h","i","j","k")
net%v%"newAttr"<-rep(NA,10)


## Single case
set.vertex.attribute(net,"newAttr","charAttr",v=which((net%v%"vertex.names")
=="f"))
net%v%"newAttr"


## Multiple case
set.vertex.attribute(net,"newAttr","charAttr2",v=which((net%v%"vertex.names"
)%in%c("a","d")))
net%v%"newAttr"


