Hi Hamid,

I'm guessing you were looking to have each undirected edge replaced with 
a mutual pair of directed edges?  Since the undirected network is being 
stored here in what amounts to upper triangle form in the sociomatrix, 
the command to change from undirected to directed won't yield that 
result; rather, you'll see the undirected edges replaced by a single 
edge in the upper-triangle.  There may be another command in network to 
do what you want to do directly, but in the meanwhile you can achieve 
the same result with an extra line of R code:

flomarriage[,] <- flomarriage[,] + t(flomarriage[,])

which drags the 1s from the upper triangle down to the lower.

Voila:

 > summary(flomarriage ~ edges + triangle)
    edges triangle
       40       24

Steve


