jeremy,

this

> FromTo<-10000*el[,1]+el[,2]

is not an optimal way to test it as you still take the directionality
of a tie into account. perhaps try with 'apply' like in the example
below. obviously your problem may be caused by something else, but it
is hard to guess without any way to reproduce the problem (e.g. small
artificial example)


> el <- matrix(c(1,2,2,3,2,1), byrow=TRUE, ncol=2) # edgelist
> el
     [,1] [,2]
[1,]    1    2
[2,]    2    3
[3,]    2    1
> u <- apply(el, 1, function(x) paste(sort(x), collapse="-"))
> u
[1] "1-2" "2-3" "1-2"
> any(duplicated(u))
[1] TRUE



~michal

