Hi all,

simulate.stergm is a bit slow. A part of this slowness  is due to the use
of the as.networkDynamic.network function
To make it faster we change the line  nw[,]<-0
by this:
# changes in nw are : mel, iel, oel
    nw$mel = lapply(1:length(nw$mel), function(x){NULL})
    nw$iel = lapply(1:length(nw$iel), function(x){integer(0)})
    nw$oel = lapply(1:length(nw$oel), function(x){integer(0)})

I don't know if these 3 lines make exactly the same changes but it works
well actually. It also resolves a problem of memory size when working with
large network.

What do you think of it? Is there something else that w[,] modify and we
did not change with our modifications?

Olivier
